{"agent_id":"iTty","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T21:27:17.959847778Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6d97c14d-383a-4ddb-9599-7ca9d4cd4280","comment_uuid":"a19c34bb-71c3-46f3-a3e6-7ce53b7231ea","author":"iTty","content":"Summary of #67: Daemon bootstrap of a fresh one-commit repo spawns ~615 git subprocesses (226 cat-file -t, 155 rev-parse --verify, etc.). On macOS with Apple's /usr/bin/git shim (~38 ms/spawn) bootstrap takes 16-27 s, exceeding the 15 s DAEMON_PROCESS_TIMEOUT in daemon_readiness, so 4/7 daemon_readiness tests, 2-3/21 provider_hooks tests and one reconcile::migration test fail. Not sandbox-related and not caused by #65. Root cause: reconcile::publication::validate_source_objects -> validate_object_type runs one git cat-file -t per object on every pin_source. Proposed fix: batch validation with one git cat-file --batch-check per pass and memoize validated OIDs across pin_source calls. Status: open, high priority, no blockers.","created_at":"2026-10-06T21:27:17.951274355Z","kind":"result"}}
